{
  "resume": "=== Abigail Rodriguez - Resume.pdf ===\nAbigail Rodriguez \nabigailro0899655@gmail.com. \nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/abigail-rodriguez-254b93202/ \n\n                                                                          929-922-1214 \nObjective  \nIt is to explore and learn from each work experience and organization to develop myself as a person and a student. \n\nLeadership Experiences \n\nGraphic Design & Content Creator for MetaBronx 2021 - Present \nMetabronx teaches students graphic design skills and then provides them a platform to \nshare their stories. \nwww.theglassfiles.com/stories  \nI write and create content on issues that affect the community. I share historical and global \nstories that are personal and meaningful to me on current events as well as personal \ninterests like country music, poems, family stories, and other creative ideas. I train younger \nstudents on how to navigate the intricate internship application process and I'm part of the \nprogram manager. \n\nVolunteer for SPEAKHIRE 2021- 2022 \nNon-profit organization that specializes in developing immigrant families to  become \nleaders in the workforce. \nspeakhire.org \nI help students with their remote learning and mentor them to be successful in their online \nclasses. \n\nVolunteer for Teen Outreach Program (TOP) at Crotona High School \nCommunity outreach program to support local teens and provide activities and resources \nfor them to get involved with their peers. \nwww.wcs.org  \nI write and record original stories for children that they can listen to at home with their \nfamilies. I help with outreach activities in the community like cleaning up the local parks \nand creating and posting flyers about upcoming events for local teens.  \n\nMentor for the Peer Group Connection (PGC) at Crotona High School  \nA teacher-run volunteer program that matches upper grades with younger students for \nnetworking and mentoring. \nwww.crotonaihs.org/for-family  \nIn the PGC leaders program we create fun and interactive programs and activities for \nyounger Crotona students using platforms like Kahoot, Padlet and others to share their \nideas and feelings and build relationships with fellow students. \n\nIntern for My bodega online  \n\nMy Bodega Online is a company that has created a platform designed for wineries that \naccelerates online ordering and delivery services. \n.http://www.mybodega.online  \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\fIn this work, a database consisting of general information about EBT stores / warehouses \nin the New York City metropolitan area was built, in which I had to use google maps to \nwalk in different counties of New York and see which bodegas are on the list and which \nones are not, just add them to the list or rank them. I even had to make calls to different \nbodegas to get essential information and see their behavior towards a customer. \n\nSkills   \n\n- \n- \n\n- \n- \n\nBilingual (Spanish and English) \nTechnology:  \n\n- \n- \n\nProficient in Adobe Spark \nProficient Google Suite \n\nStorytelling: I have written for Glass Files and produced children’s stories for Teen Outreach program.  \nPublic speaking: I recently presented to a class of 25+ students on my involvement in the PGC mentorship \nprogram. \n\n-  Overall, I am Christian,extremely studious and dedicated  \n\nAbout Me \nSoy genuinamente creyente en Dios  y me gusta escribir historias “Jugar con  la imaginación y la realidad” \n. Actualmente  participo en la organización llamada Meta Bronx en las que me dirijo a diferentes escuelas a hablar de \nmis experiencias y motivar a los estudiantes de esta generación “ A hacer lo que el 99% no hace”  \n\nMotivando a estudiantes que no tienen un inglés fluido en el que el lenguaje se nos hace una barrera sin embargo \nutilizar esa debilidad como un trampolín y desafiarte a ti mismo , es algo que me ha ayudado en mi crecimiento \npersonal.",
